  ('english', 'subject-verb-agreement', 'Fill in the blank: Neither the pilot nor the crew members ___ aware of the change in schedule.', 'were', 'was', 'has been', 'is', 'A', 'With neither…nor, the verb agrees with the nearer subject. ''Crew members'' is plural, so ''were''.', 'Subject-verb agreement', 'exam', '{}'),
  ('english', 'tenses', 'Fill in the blank: By the time we reached the airport, the flight ___.', 'left', 'had left', 'was leaving', 'has left', 'B', 'The earlier of two past actions takes the past perfect: had left.', 'Past perfect tense', 'moderate', '{}'),
  ('english', 'active-passive', 'Choose the passive form: The controller cleared the aircraft for take-off.', 'The aircraft had been cleared for take-off by the controller.', 'The aircraft is cleared for take-off by the controller.', 'The aircraft was cleared for take-off by the controller.', 'The aircraft was being cleared for take-off by the controller.', 'C', 'Simple past active (cleared) becomes was + past participle (was cleared).', 'Active and passive voice', 'moderate', '{}'),
