  ('quant', 'partnership', 'A invests ₹40,000 for 12 months and B invests ₹60,000 for 6 months. Out of a profit of ₹21,000, A''s share is:', '₹9,000', '₹12,000', '₹14,000', '₹10,500', 'B', 'Ratio = 40000×12 : 60000×6 = 4 : 3. A''s share = 4/7 × 21000 = ₹12,000.', 'Partnership', 'exam', '{}'),
  ('quant', 'ages', 'A father is three times as old as his son. After 12 years he will be twice as old as the son. The father''s present age is:', '30 years', '48 years', '36 years', '42 years', 'C', 'Let son = s: 3s + 12 = 2(s + 12), so s = 12 and the father is 36.', 'Problems on ages', 'moderate', '{}'),
  ('quant', 'mixture-alligation', 'In what ratio must rice at ₹40/kg be mixed with rice at ₹55/kg to get a mixture worth ₹45/kg?', '1 : 2', '3 : 1', '1 : 1', '2 : 1', 'D', 'Alligation: (55 − 45) : (45 − 40) = 10 : 5 = 2 : 1.', 'Alligation', 'exam', '{}'),
