  ('management', 'fayol-principles', '"An employee should receive orders from only one superior" is Fayol''s principle of:', 'Unity of direction', 'Unity of command', 'Scalar chain', 'Centralisation', 'B', 'Unity of command = one boss. Unity of direction = one head and one plan for a group of activities with the same objective.', 'Unity of command', 'moderate', '{}'),
  ('management', 'fayol-principles', 'Fayol''s concept of ''gang plank'' is related to the principle of:', 'Unity of command', 'Order', 'Scalar chain', 'Equity', 'C', 'The gang plank allows direct communication between same-level employees, as a shortcut in the scalar chain.', 'Scalar chain', 'exam', '{}'),
  ('management', 'bureaucracy', 'The bureaucratic model of organisation is associated with:', 'Chester Barnard', 'Abraham Maslow', 'Peter Drucker', 'Max Weber', 'D', 'Max Weber proposed bureaucracy based on rules, hierarchy and impersonality.', 'Bureaucracy', 'easy', '{}'),
  ('management', 'human-relations', 'The Hawthorne experiments, which led to the human relations approach, were conducted by:', 'Elton Mayo', 'Douglas McGregor', 'F. W. Taylor', 'Henry Gantt', 'A', 'Elton Mayo and colleagues found that social and psychological factors affect productivity.', 'Hawthorne studies', 'moderate', '{}'),
